From: y52s recovery work
Subject: [PATCH] y52s: verify with the gatekeeper handle an app-clone escrow key
 is really bound to

A user can hold more than one gatekeeper enrolment.  On this device user 0
has two, and the app-clone keystore escrow entry is bound to the SID of the
one stored as the plaintext spblob/0000000000000000.handle, while TWRP only
ever tried the handle embedded in the .pwd file.  Every begin() therefore
returned KEY_USER_NOT_AUTHENTICATED (-26) no matter which SID was patched in
afterwards: the token was never wrong, it was signed for the other enrolment.

Try the plaintext handle first and fall back to the .pwd one when gatekeeper
rejects it, logging which handle was accepted.  The two handles are compared
byte for byte, not by length, so a single-enrolment device takes exactly the
old path once and nothing changes for it.
---
